From 3e8691e0bc9d400532943cea93962882ed4d696e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:16:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] S3-1: the sim's resident pass is spread over the whole
 15 game minutes

All 1,000 residents came due in the same 32 ticks every 15 game minutes (every stamp is set to the same
minute by sim_init, a load and a fast-forward, and the round robin took 32 slots a tick): 10-15 ms of extra
work in each of those ticks on the GBA, 17 frames of 50-67 ms on every free-play screen every 37.7 s.
Now the cursor earns slots with the clock, 1,000 per SIM_INTERVAL (15) game minutes whatever the day
length and speed options (SIM_PASS_NUM / SIM_PASS_DEN, a credit in the padding of SimState: no new RAM), so
a resident is updated once per interval and a tick does one update at the default clock (15 at the
fastest). SIM_BATCH (the hard cap of a tick) is 16. A visit that would live fewer than SIM_PASS_MIN (8) game
minutes (the first pass after sim_init, a load or a fast-forward) leaves the stamp alone, so the next visit
lives all the minutes: none lost, none counted twice. Fast-forward is unchanged (15 minutes, hour chunks).

test_sim_pass.c: once per interval and one update a tick at the default clock, the first passes after a
load and a fast-forward (no burst, nobody waits more than 1.5 intervals), every day length and speed,
determinism. The sim goldens that depend on the order of the updates are recorded again on purpose
(test_sim_x4: freeplay, story possession, fast-forward; test_sim: the news stream 16,575 -> 16,629 bytes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
